{"ref":"BDB, הוֹשֵׁעַ²","hw":"הוֹשֵׁעַ²","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">הוֹשֵׁעַ</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. (</strong><em>salvation;</em> on form, cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַשְׁמֵד</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">הַמְשֵׁל</span>; on pronunciation v. Hpt<sup>ZA ii, 261 Anm. 2</sup> Jäger<sup>BAS i, 468</sup><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>1.</strong>  orig. name of Joshua according to <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:8\" href=\"/Numbers.13.8\">Nu 13:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:16\" href=\"/Numbers.13.16\">16</a> (P), 𝔊 Αυση, cf. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 32:44\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.32.44\">Dt 32:44</a> (J; prob. error, v. Dr), 𝔊 Ιησους, v. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, יְהוֹשׁוּעַ\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_יְהוֹשׁוּעַ\">יְהוֹשׁוּעַ</a> p. 221 supr.<br><strong>2.</strong>  last king of Israel <a data-ref=\"II Kings 15:30\" href=\"/II_Kings.15.30\">2 K 15:30</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:1\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.1\">17:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:3\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.3\">3</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:4\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:6\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.6\">6</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 18:1\" href=\"/II_Kings.18.1\">18:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 18:9\" href=\"/II_Kings.18.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 18:10\" href=\"/II_Kings.18.10\">10</a>, 𝔊 Ωσηε.<br><strong>3.</strong>  the prophet Hosea <a data-ref=\"Hosea 1:1\" href=\"/Hosea.1.1\">Ho 1:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Hosea 1:2\" href=\"/Hosea.1.2\">2</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, 𝔊 Ωσηε.<br><strong>4.</strong>  an Ephraimite chief under David <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 27:20\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.27.20\">1 Ch 27:20</a>, 𝔊 Ωση(ε).<br><strong>5.</strong>  a chief under Nehemiah <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 10:24\" href=\"/Nehemiah.10.24\">Ne 10:24</a>, 𝔊 Ωσηθα, Ωσηε.","next":"BDB, הוֹשַׁעֲיָה","prev":"BDB, יְשַׁעְיָה"}